      {
        "id": "p31-q92-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Prove that $\\dfrac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-1}-\\dfrac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta+1}=2\\tan\\theta$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p31-q92-a-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The identity holds where ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\sin\\theta\\ne0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\cos\\theta\\ne0",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p31-q92-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Combine over a common denominator and use ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta-1=\\cot^2\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " to reduce the left-hand side to ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "2\\tan\\theta",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The original expressions require $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$ and $\\cos\\theta\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-1}-\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta+1}&=\\frac{\\cot\\theta[(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta+1)-(\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-1)]}{\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta-1}\\\\\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-1}-\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta+1}&=\\frac{2\\cot\\theta}{\\cot^2\\theta}\\\\\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-1}-\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta+1}&=\\frac{2}{\\cot\\theta}\\\\\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-1}-\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta+1}&=\\frac{2\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}\\\\\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta-1}-\\frac{\\cot\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}\\theta+1}&=2\\tan\\theta.\\end{align*}$$\nCancellation is valid on this domain because $\\cot\\theta\\ne0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q92-b",
